<div id="view_text_dialog" class="forminput" style="display:none;">
	
	For quick copying and pasting to a text based forum or email.<br/>
	<textarea style="width: 97%; height: 100%; max-height: 280px; font-size: 1.2em;" readonly="readonly" tabindex="-1">HOME BREW RECIPE:
Title: Vanilla Cream Ale
Author: Stikks     2-2-12

Brew Method: All Grain
Style Name: Cream Ale
Boil Time: 75 min
Batch Size: 5.75 gallons (fermentor volume)
Boil Size: 7.5 gallons
Boil Gravity: 1.038
Efficiency: 70% (brew house)


STATS:
Original Gravity: 1.055
Final Gravity: 1.013
ABV (standard): 5.48%
IBU (tinseth): 19.44
SRM (morey): 4.83
Mash pH: 

FERMENTABLES:
5.25 lb - Pale 2-Row (44.7%)
2 lb - White Wheat (17%)
2 lb - Pale 6-Row (17%)
0.5 lb - Flaked Corn (4.3%)
0.5 lb - Caramel / Crystal 20L (4.3%)
0.5 lb - Carapils (Dextrine Malt) (4.3%)
0.25 lb - Flaked Barley (2.1%)
0.75 lb - Honey - (late boil kettle addition)  (6.4%)

HOPS:
0.5 oz - Cascade, Type: Pellet, AA: 6.2, Use: Boil for 60 min, IBU: 11.42
0.5 oz - Cascade, Type: Pellet, AA: 6.2, Use: Boil for 20 min, IBU: 6.92
0.5 oz - saaz, Type: Pellet, AA: 3, Use: Boil for 5 min, IBU: 1.1

OTHER INGREDIENTS:
2 oz - pure vanilla extract, Type: Flavor, Use: Boil
1 oz - pure vanilla extract, Type: Flavor, Use: Bottling
1 tsp - yeast nutrient, Time: 15 min, Type: Other, Use: Boil
1 each - whirlfloc, Time: 15 min, Type: Fining, Use: Boil
4 each - Vanilla beans - in 2oz Vodka, Type: Other, Use: Secondary

YEAST:
Wyeast - Kölsch 2565
Starter: Yes
Form: Liquid
Attenuation (custom): 76%
Flocculation: Low
Optimum Temp: 56 - 70 F
Fermentation Temp: 64 F

PRIMING:
Method: corn sugar
Amount: 4.5 oz
CO2 Level: 2.65 Volumes

TARGET WATER PROFILE:
Profile Name: bottled spring water
Ca2: 0
Mg2: 0
Na: 0
Cl: 0
SO4: 0
HCO3: 0

MASH GUIDELINES:
1) Infusion, Start Temp: -- F, Target Temp: 168 F, Time: 75 min, Amount: 15 qt, rest at 150
2) Infusion, Start Temp: -- F, Target Temp: 212 F, Time: 15 min, Amount: 7 qt, stir and rest at 165 - mashout
3) Fly Sparge, Start Temp: -- F, Target Temp: 170 F, Time: 45 min, Amount: 18 qt, to volume-7.5 gal.

WATER REQUIREMENTS:
Strike water volume at mash thickness of 1.75 qt/lb, 4.81gal (19.3qt)
Mash volume with grains, 5.69gal (22.8qt)
Grain absorption losses, -1.38gal (-5.5qt)
Remaining sparge water volume (equipment estimates 4.44 g | 17.7 qt), 4.31gal (17.3qt)
Mash Lauter Tun losses, -0.25gal (-1qt)
Pre boil volume (equipment estimates 7.62 g | 30.5 qt), 7.5gal (30qt)
Volume increase from sugar/extract (late additions), 0.06gal (0.2qt)
Boil off losses, -1.88gal (-7.5qt)
Hops absorption losses (first wort, boil, aroma), -0.06gal (-0.2qt)
Post boil Volume, 5.75gal (23qt)
Going into fermentor, 5.75gal (23qt)

Total Water Needed: 9.13gal (36.5qt)

NOTES:
1600 ml. starter at 1.04

Ferment at 58 to 60 degrees with
Wyeast 2565,62 to 64 degrees with WLP 029
or 65 to 67 degrees with US-05

attenuation better than expected
finished at 1.011 about 5.3 ABV

carbonate 3 weeks at 68-70 degrees
cold condition 1 week in fridge
frothy head,nice lacing 

tasty summer beer,easy drinking.
A great beer for the female in your life.

I`ve made this brew 7 times now,and it is a mainstay for my woman.I`ve used US-05
WLP 029 and WYEAST 2565 all with great 
results.Used Williamette in place of
saaz and prefer it.Last batch came out
at 6.0 ABV with a modification to my fly sparge setup.Grain bill holds at 11 lbs.

Last batch was with WLP 029,I think Wyeast 2565 was the best of the 3 yeast types that I have used. (just me and swmbo`s thoughts).

Made batch #8 with US-05 on 4-19-13
used 4 Madagascar vanilla beans soaked 
in vodka for a week and added to secondary
It added a bit more vanilla flavor.Nice addition for added flavor.Will make this
a regular step in future batches,recipe
has not changed but 2565 rules the brew.

I made batch #9 on 9-22-13.Used original recipe with wyeast 2565, by far the best.
Bottled on 11-1-2013.The only tweak was 
adding 12 oz clover honey at flameout.The
Vanilla beans in secondary are the bomb.
Recipe will not change from here on out.
This batch started at 1.057 and finished at 1.01 - 5.51 ABV.It is exactly where I Want it. SWMBO and my friends love it.I like it alot too but I am more of a stout
porter guy.I hope you like it and have good luck with it if you try it. -enjoy- 

12-8-2013 Vanilla flavor has mellowed
nicely,lacing last`s till the end of the glass.Very pleased with this batch.

Batch #10 1-23-2015 recipe has not changed
will be bottling in about a week or so.
This brew is our house brew all year,it`s
one for the ladies.Will be ready for St.
Paddy`s day.

batch #10 is long gone.Finally retired and will be moving to Florida in 2 weeks.I will update next batch when I brew in in the heat for the first time,Goodbye Chicago.I hope you enjoy the recipe.-Will be back to brewing soon.

-Cheers-










