lspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/avatars/2020_02/303867_rzgl0dypxp_sm.jpg" alt="Brewer profile picture"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/303867'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>Themad</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 02/18/2020 at 02:06pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Great idea! I tasted similar cream ale in Dublin, it was a crazy combination to create beer and have not tried the best.</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/231724'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>mujin</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 03/10/2020 at 12:41pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'></font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/231724'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>mujin</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 03/10/2020 at 12:42pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Would anyone who&#039;s brewed this cite a target water profile?</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/312957'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>slubbbiii</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 03/20/2020 at 11:20am</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'></font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/321184'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>KEVINSKENE</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 06/09/2020 at 03:15pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Really looking forward to brewing this beer! It&acirc;&euro;&trade;ll be my first step mash and i had a question..<BR><BR>When you raise the temp, are you just dumping in your 7qts of boiling water, if not, about how long are you taking to raise the temp?  <BR><BR>Also, any suggestions for minerals if starting with distilled water?<BR><BR>Really looking forward to this one.</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/avatars/2012_12/116_xxftxz5sq5_sm.jpg" alt="Brewer profile picture"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/116'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>stikks</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 06/10/2020 at 12:00pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Thanks for ? Kevin.For the 7 gal boiling water I pour in slowly while stirring constantly to bring mash up<BR>to mashout temp 170 and then fly sparge.As for as water goes I just use bottled spring water no other additions of minerals as spring water contains any minerals needed as far as I`m concerned.Hope this helps.-Cheers</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/332246'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>Hoodick</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 11/13/2020 at 04:01pm</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>This is a fantastic recipe. Never disappoints. I&acirc;&euro;&trade;ve brewed this twice. I did a 90 min boil and started my additions at 75min. Recommend doing a yeast starter. I used WLP029. I got an OG at 1.060 both times and a FG of 1.005 with a 7% ABV. Make sure you soak the vanilla beans in the vodka for two weeks while the beer is fermenting. This way you can add to the secondary. I keg after two more weeks and add another ounce of vanilla. If bottling use 5.5 oz of printing (corn) sugar since this will yield 5.5 to 6 gallons. This beer disappears quickly.</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/323309'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>Kylert1</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 05/02/2021 at 07:16am</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Followed recipe and it came out really nice. I tasted at bottling and it was a bit sweet so I decided not to add the last 2 oz of vanilla. Now that the beer has been in bottle for a month, I regret not adding those last 2 ounces. There&#039;s a nice balance of hop and vanilla but if I didn&#039;t tell you, you wouldn&#039;t know it has vanilla. Next time I&#039;ll add those last 2. Aloha from Hawaii</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/366174'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>Brewer Peter</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 10/29/2021 at 12:46pm</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>hi stikks, thank you for sharing this recipe which i haven&#039;t prepared yet but i plan to make soon. I know it&#039;s been a long time since this recipe was published but if you find yourself reading this message I hope you can answer me. I wanted to ask you 2 questions:<BR>1) I have read that you have used different yeasts, I am a beginner and I have not yet mastered liquid yeasts and I would like to use US-05, how do you like the final result of beer with this yeast?<BR>2) I didn&#039;t understand how and how many times you add vanilla? If I have not misunderstood, take 4 vanilla pods and once you have opened and removed the pulp, let them macerate in 2 oz of volka for 2 weeks and pour the contents at the end of boiling as soon as you turn off the heat, then repeat the operation during the secondary. and finally 1 ounce before bottling? so in total you use 10 vanilla pods and 5 ounces of vodka? I hope to receive your reply. thank you very much, best regards.</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/381503'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>Beer1</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 08/29/2022 at 02:11pm</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'></font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/avatars/2022_09/381716_2kcxjxxkx0_sm.jpg" alt="Brewer profile picture"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/381716'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>beer4thewin</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 09/02/2022 at 02:44pm</font><br><div class='reviews'><ul style='list-style: outside none none;'><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li><li><span class='active'></span></li></ul><span><span class='blue'> 5 of 5 </span></div><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Thank you for sharing this amazing recipe!</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/avatars/2020_01/1653_xzhf5ncxbq_sm.jpg" alt="Brewer profile picture"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/1653'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>prospero</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 06/17/2026 at 05:32pm</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>A few questions:<BR>It seems the wheat and crystal would exceed maximums that could be detrimental to head retention and also cause chill haze.  What has been the result most people have seen?  Bad/Good/Great head retention?  Clear or Chill haze?  Why was wheat added?  It seems it would add body but then the lower mash temp suggests the goal was a drier/thinner body beer?  Just curious as a few things seem to contradict each other.  Sounds like a great beer and I&#039;m hoping to brew a version of this, so any tips appreciated!</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR></td></tr></table></div><div style='clear:both;'></div>
	

	
