<script type="application/ld+json">
{
    "@context": "https://schema.org/",
    "@type": "Recipe",
    "name": "Vanilla Cream Ale",
    "description": "1600 ml. starter at 1.04\r\n\r\nFerment at 58 to 60 degrees with\r\nWyeast 2565,62 to 64 degrees with WLP 029\r\nor 65 to 67 degrees with US-05\r\n\r\nattenuation better than expected\r\nfinished at 1.011 about 5.3 ABV\r\n\r\ncarbonate 3 weeks at 68-70 degrees\r\ncold condition 1 week in fridge\r\nfrothy head,nice lacing \r\n\r\ntasty summer beer,easy drinking.\r\nA great beer for the female in your life.\r\n\r\nI`ve made this brew 7 times now,and it is a mainstay for my woman.I`ve used US-05\r\nWLP 029 and WYEAST 2565 all with great \r\nresults.Used Williamette in place of\r\nsaaz and prefer it.Last batch came out\r\nat 6.0 ABV with a modification to my fly sparge setup.Grain bill holds at 11 lbs.\r\n\r\nLast batch was with WLP 029,I think Wyeast 2565 was the best of the 3 yeast types that I have used. (just me and swmbo`s thoughts).\r\n\r\nMade batch #8 with US-05 on 4-19-13\r\nused 4 Madagascar vanilla beans soaked \r\nin vodka for a week and added to secondary\r\nIt added a bit more vanilla flavor.Nice addition for added flavor.Will make this\r\na regular step in future batches,recipe\r\nhas not changed but 2565 rules the brew.\r\n\r\nI made batch #9 on 9-22-13.Used original recipe with wyeast 2565, by far the best.\r\nBottled on 11-1-2013.The only tweak was \r\nadding 12 oz clover honey at flameout.The\r\nVanilla beans in secondary are the bomb.\r\nRecipe will not change from here on out.\r\nThis batch started at 1.057 and finished at 1.01 - 5.51 ABV.It is exactly where I Want it. SWMBO and my friends love it.I like it alot too but I am more of a stout\r\nporter guy.I hope you like it and have good luck with it if you try it. -enjoy- \r\n\r\n12-8-2013 Vanilla flavor has mellowed\r\nnicely,lacing last`s till the end of the glass.Very pleased with this batch.\r\n\r\nBatch #10 1-23-2015 recipe has not changed\r\nwill be bottling in about a week or so.\r\nThis brew is our house brew all year,it`s\r\none for the ladies.Will be ready for St.\r\nPaddy`s day.\r\n\r\nbatch #10 is long gone.Finally retired and will be moving to Florida in 2 weeks.I will update next batch when I brew in in the heat for the first time,Goodbye Chicago.I hope you enjoy the recipe.-Will be back to brewing soon.\r\n\r\n-Cheers-",
    "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "stikks"
    },
    "datePublished": "2012-01-31",
    "image": [
        "https://www.brewersfriend.com/avatars/2012_12/116_xxftxz5sq5_lg.jpg"
    ],
    "recipeCategory": "Cream Ale",
    "recipeCuisine": "Homebrewing",
    "recipeYield": "5.75 gallons",
    "prepTime": "PT135M",
    "cookTime": "PT75M",
    "totalTime": "PT210M",
    "nutrition": {
        "@type": "NutritionInformation",
        "servingSize": "12 oz",
        "calories": "181 calories",
        "carbohydrateContent": "18.2 g"
    },
    "recipeIngredient": [
        "5.25 lb Pale 2-Row",
        "2 lb White Wheat",
        "2 lb Pale 6-Row",
        "0.5 lb Flaked Corn",
        "0.5 lb Caramel / Crystal 20L",
        "0.5 lb Carapils (Dextrine Malt)",
        "0.25 lb Flaked Barley",
        "0.75 lb Honey",
        "0.5 oz Cascade Hops",
        "0.5 oz Cascade Hops",
        "0.5 oz saaz Hops"
    ],
    "recipeInstructions": [
        {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "name": "Mash",
            "text": "Mash (rest at 150) — Infusion at 168°F for 75 minutes."
        },
        {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "name": "Mash",
            "text": "Mash (stir and rest at 165 - mashout) — Infusion at 212°F for 15 minutes."
        },
        {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "name": "Mash",
            "text": "Mash (to volume-7.5 gal.) — Fly Sparge at 170°F for 45 minutes."
        },
        {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "name": "Boil",
            "text": "Bring wort to a boil and boil for 75 minutes. Add hops: Cascade (Boil 60 min); Cascade (Boil 20 min); saaz (Boil 5 min)."
        },
        {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "name": "Ferment",
            "text": "Ferment with Wyeast Kölsch 2565 at 64°F."
        }
    ],
    "aggregateRating": {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        "ratingValue": 4.8,
        "reviewCount": 21
    }
